# P2-D3 — Shell orchestration symbol rename

Phase 2 Lane R neutralized **filenames**. Residual **P2-D3** renames remaining **hand-written shell** exports that still carry `Denali*` / `useDenali*` while behaving as generic operator wizard chrome.

## Tranche P2-D3.a (this slice)

Rename map (shell only):

| Legacy | New |
| ------ | --- |
| `DenaliCreateTourWizardClient` | `OperatorCreateTourWizardClient` |
| `DenaliFlatEditPageClient` | `OperatorFlatEditPageClient` |
| `useDenaliCreateTourWizard` | `useOperatorCreateTourWizard` |
| `useDenaliFlatEditPage` | `useOperatorFlatEditPage` |
| `DenaliFlatEditPageShell` / `DenaliFlatEditPageHeader` | `OperatorFlatEditPageShell` / `OperatorFlatEditPageHeader` |
| Shell wrapper `DenaliFlatEditForm` | `OperatorFlatEditForm` |

Routers (`NewTourWizardClient`, `TourEditPageClient`) keep plugin-id branching; they now call `Operator*` clients.

## Non-goals (deferred at P2-D3.a; status)

- Generated bootstrap chrome symbols — **Phase 4j:** create/flat-edit chrome binders export
  `useOperator*` / `loadOperator*` / `Operator*` only (no shell `useDenali*` chrome aliases).
  Residual generated product tokens may remain on other binders (forms, views) until capability host.
- `DENALI_PLUGIN_ID` / tenant fixtures — product identity
- `DenaliLogoMark` — P2-D2
- `messages.denali` — P2-D3.b
- Package exports under `@app-cloud/workspace-denali`

## Invariant

Shell public chrome API is `Operator*`. Product packages may still export `Denali*` internals;
shell codegen must not dual-export Denali+Operator aliases for the same wrapper.

Authority: `TEMP/phases/P2-denali-extraction-plan.md` § P2-D3.a.
